namespace sandbox.api

import jo.IO.stdout
import harpe.caps.*

// The agent's contract: the entry point the LLM implements each turn, and the
// capabilities it receives. Grant more by declaring capability params and widening
// `receives`; the implementations are built in the runtime, the LLM only gets the
// capability.

// The capability params (`fs`, the format backends, `image`, `ocr`) are the
// standard ones declared in the caps module — the same set the web driver grants.
// `fs` is the chat's data directory (`data/<chat>/`) as a confined tree the guest
// reads and writes via `Path`: how the agent reads files the user sent and writes
// files to send back. Its openPDF/openWorkbook/openWord shortcuts go through the
// pdfReader/excelReader/wordReader backends, which the runtime binds.
defer def runTask(): Unit receives stdout, fs, pdfReader, excelReader, wordReader, image, ocr
